WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.300
A crowd.

2
00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.970
Someone holds out a gold
circlet to a robed figure.

3
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.630
He pushes it away.

4
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:07.620
Once.

5
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.580
Twice.

6
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.940
Three times.

7
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:15.250
And every time, "the rabblement
hooted, and clapp’d their chopt hands".

8
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.030
Yet one man who was watching
tells the story his own way.

9
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.880
Three refusals.

10
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.940
So why does everyone call him ambitious?

11
00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.690
In this mission, you'll find out why
king was an explosive word in Rome,

12
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.390
after its people drove out their last one.

13
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.690
You'll see why it mattered that, in 44 BC,

14
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.540
Caesar was named dictator for life.

15
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.070
And you'll gather the
evidence on both sides,

16
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.750
up to Antony's claim: "Ambition
should be made of sterner stuff".

17
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.970
Your mission: decide whether the play
ever proves that Caesar is ambitious.
